# Provider Routing Rules

OpenAI is the default provider, but Atticus must support OpenAI, Claude, and Gemini through one common interface.

Do not let app code directly call provider SDKs. All provider-specific logic belongs in `atticus/providers/`.

Provider interface should support:

- text generation;
- future streaming;
- future tool-calling abstraction;
- provider-specific model names in config;
- graceful missing-key errors;
- timeouts/retries;
- usage metadata when available.

Default router behavior in v0.1:

- Use OpenAI unless The Speaker explicitly requests another provider.
- Include a `ProviderRouter` class with a simple strategy hook for future automatic routing.

Future router hints:

- General work: OpenAI.
- Long-form writing/review: Claude candidate.
- Multimodal/Google ecosystem tasks: Gemini candidate.
- Always allow manual override.
- Privacy gate must run before provider call if user files are included.
